{"book":15,"chapter":18,"rubric":"OPERATIONS AND SECURITY / CHAPTER 18","slides":[{"title":"Two sets of techniques","sub":"SSH and VPN","short":"SSH and VPN","main":"SSH is a secure shell and port forwarding; VPN is an encrypted tunnel between networks.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["SSH","VPN","Tasks","Plan"],"captions":["SSH is a secure remote shell and port forwarding","A VPN is an encrypted tunnel carrying packets of private networks","One for administration, the other for linking offices and remote staff","In this chapter: trust, keys, bastion, office tunnel, MTU, and split tunnel"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":90.0,"y":55.0,"w":140.0,"h":44.0,"text":"SSH\nsecure shell\nand port forwarding","tone":"green","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v","x":270.0,"y":55.0,"w":140.0,"h":44.0,"text":"VPN\nencrypted tunnel\nbetween networks","tone":"yellow","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5,"o":0.25}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":90.0,"y":55.0,"w":140.0,"h":44.0,"text":"SSH\nsecure shell\nand port forwarding","tone":"green","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v","x":270.0,"y":55.0,"w":140.0,"h":44.0,"text":"VPN\nencrypted tunnel\nbetween networks","tone":"yellow","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":90.0,"y":55.0,"w":140.0,"h":44.0,"text":"SSH\nsecure shell\nand port forwarding","tone":"green","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v","x":270.0,"y":55.0,"w":140.0,"h":44.0,"text":"VPN\nencrypted tunnel\nbetween networks","tone":"yellow","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t3","x":90.0,"y":100.0,"text":"administration","tone":"green","size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t3b","x":270.0,"y":100.0,"text":"offices and staff","tone":"yellow","size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":90.0,"y":55.0,"w":140.0,"h":44.0,"text":"SSH\nsecure shell\nand port forwarding","tone":"green","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v","x":270.0,"y":55.0,"w":140.0,"h":44.0,"text":"VPN\nencrypted tunnel\nbetween networks","tone":"yellow","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t3","x":90.0,"y":100.0,"text":"administration","tone":"green","size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t3b","x":270.0,"y":100.0,"text":"offices and staff","tone":"yellow","size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t4","x":180.0,"y":140.0,"text":"keys · bastion · tunnels · routes · MTU","tone":"blue","size":9.5}]],"cues":[12.1,19.3,26.0]},{"t":"note","text":"One is for administration, the other for linking offices."}]},{"title":"SSH","sub":"Instead of telnet","short":"SSH","main":"SSH encrypts the session and verifies the server; port 22 is scanned constantly, so protection is a must.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["The old way","SSH","Features","Cost of openness"],"captions":["Telnet and rlogin sent the password in clear text","SSH encrypts the whole session and verifies the server","Port 22; besides the shell: files and tunnels for other protocols","So an open port 22 is constantly scanned and hit with password guessing"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":90.0,"y":40.0,"w":130.0,"h":26.0,"text":"telnet: clear password","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":90.0,"y":40.0,"w":130.0,"h":26.0,"text":"telnet: clear password","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"a","x1":150.0,"y1":40.0,"x2":215.0,"y2":40.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":280.0,"y":40.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"SSH: encryption","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":90.0,"y":40.0,"w":130.0,"h":26.0,"text":"telnet: clear password","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"a","x1":150.0,"y1":40.0,"x2":215.0,"y2":40.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":280.0,"y":40.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"SSH: encryption","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t3","x":180.0,"y":85.0,"text":"port 22 · files (scp, sftp) · tunnels","tone":"yellow","size":9.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":90.0,"y":40.0,"w":130.0,"h":26.0,"text":"telnet: clear password","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"a","x1":150.0,"y1":40.0,"x2":215.0,"y2":40.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":280.0,"y":40.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"SSH: encryption","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t3","x":180.0,"y":85.0,"text":"port 22 · files (scp, sftp) · tunnels","tone":"yellow","size":9.0},{"t":"text","id":"t4","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"open port 22 is scanned and guessed constantly","tone":"red","size":8.5}]],"cues":[6.6,19.5,26.3]},{"t":"note","text":"Plus files (scp, sftp) and tunnels."}]},{"title":"Host key","sub":"Trust on first use","short":"Host key","main":"The first login remembers the server key in known_hosts; if it changes, the client warns loudly.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Fingerprint","Trust","Changed","Check"],"captions":["On first connection the client shows the host key fingerprint","The accepted key is saved in known_hosts: trust on first use","If the key has changed, the client warns loudly","Either the key was changed or the server was replaced: find out first, then delete the entry"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":15.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["$ ssh alice@10.0.0.5","The authenticity of host can't be","established. Fingerprint SHA256:ab12…","Trust? yes","→ entry in known_hosts"],"hl":[1],"lang":"plain","size":8.5,"lh":13.0,"w":270.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":15.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["$ ssh alice@10.0.0.5","The authenticity of host can't be","established. Fingerprint SHA256:ab12…","Trust? yes","→ entry in known_hosts"],"hl":[3],"lang":"plain","size":8.5,"lh":13.0,"w":270.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":15.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["$ ssh alice@10.0.0.5","The authenticity of host can't be","established. Fingerprint SHA256:ab12…","Trust? yes","→ entry in known_hosts"],"hl":[3],"lang":"plain","size":8.5,"lh":13.0,"w":270.0},{"t":"text","id":"t3","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"later: key changed → WARNING: HOST IDENTIFICATION CHANGED","tone":"red","size":8.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":15.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["$ ssh alice@10.0.0.5","The authenticity of host can't be","established. Fingerprint SHA256:ab12…","Trust? yes","→ entry in known_hosts"],"hl":[3],"lang":"plain","size":8.5,"lh":13.0,"w":270.0},{"t":"text","id":"t3","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"later: key changed → WARNING: HOST IDENTIFICATION CHANGED","tone":"red","size":8.0},{"t":"text","id":"t4","x":180.0,"y":132.0,"text":"ask the admin: planned change or MITM?","tone":"yellow","size":9.0},{"t":"text","id":"t4b","x":180.0,"y":150.0,"text":"and only then: ssh-keygen -R","tone":"green","size":9.0}]],"cues":[6.3,18.6,31.2]},{"t":"note","text":"A warning is a reason to check, not to silence."}]},{"title":"Login keys","sub":"Instead of passwords","short":"Login keys","main":"The private key stays with you, the public one goes to authorized_keys; then password login is turned off.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Key pair","Copying","Signature","No passwords"],"captions":["ssh-keygen makes a pair: the private part stays with you","The public one is copied to the server, to the list of allowed keys","Key login: the client proves it owns the private key with a signature","After checking, password authentication on the server is turned off"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":70.0,"y":40.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"private key\nwith you","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"u","x":290.0,"y":40.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"public key\nauthorized_keys","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5,"o":0.25}],[{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":70.0,"y":40.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"private key\nwith you","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"u","x":290.0,"y":40.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"public key\nauthorized_keys","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"c","x1":126.0,"y1":40.0,"x2":232.0,"y2":40.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"t2","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"text":"ssh-copy-id","size":8.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":70.0,"y":40.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"private key\nwith you","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"u","x":290.0,"y":40.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"public key\nauthorized_keys","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"c","x1":126.0,"y1":40.0,"x2":232.0,"y2":40.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"t2","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"text":"ssh-copy-id","size":8.0,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"t3","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"text":"client proves by signature: no secret on the wire","tone":"green","size":9.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":70.0,"y":40.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"private key\nwith you","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"u","x":290.0,"y":40.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"public key\nauthorized_keys","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"c","x1":126.0,"y1":40.0,"x2":232.0,"y2":40.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"t2","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"text":"ssh-copy-id","size":8.0,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"t3","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"text":"client proves by signature: no secret on the wire","tone":"green","size":9.0},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"w":260.0,"h":22.0,"text":"PasswordAuthentication no  — passwords off","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[6.5,20.1,26.9]},{"t":"note","text":"No secret crosses the network."}]},{"title":"Bastion and forwarding","sub":"Jump and tunnel","short":"Bastion","main":"Through a bastion with ssh -J; port forwarding is handy but opens the whole network from the server.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Jump","To the target","Forwarding","Careful"],"captions":["Only one node is open to the outside, the bastion; the client logs in to it","...and from there reaches internal servers that are not published outside","Port forwarding makes a remote service available on a local port","A handy but potentially dangerous mechanism: any service on the network 